cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Cite this software release using the metadata below. The DOI identifies software,
  not the manuscript.
type: software
title: 'Conditional flow matching in acute human wounds: analysis software'
authors:
- family-names: Fu
  given-names: Zeyu
version: 0.4.2
license: MIT
abstract: Analysis software for a three-donor audit of population reconstruction by
  conditional flow matching in acute human wounds. Product-coupled fields operate
  in a frozen 15-dimensional expression representation. The study distinguishes global
  time holdout from donor transfer and compares endpoint controls, training-target
  marginals, paired clocks, distribution shape and observed expression. Simple permitted-data
  predictors outperform flow in important comparisons. The study does not identify
  individual cell trajectories or validate clinical wound prognosis.
repository-code: https://github.com/PeterPonyu/wound-population-dynamics
keywords:
- single-cell transcriptomics
- wound healing
- population dynamics
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22962339
